CODEGEN.md §3.5, §5.13, §6.1, DECISIONS 203: in a go types emit, a record whose @go(name:) takes another type's name collides once: the decode<T> built on the two classes' one Go name comes from the same pair of declarations, named by their Canon names, so no second E8005 names the package.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// X.
record X {
  /// N.
  n: Int
}

/// Y.
record Y @go(name: "X") {
  /// N.
  n: Int
}

/// An enum.
enum Color { red }

/// Z.
record Z @go(name: "Color") {
  /// N.
  n: Int
}

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a", mode: types }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  a/a.canon:10:8
  go: X is generated for both a.X and a.Y; rename one of them with @go(name:)

error[E8005]  a/a.canon:19:8
  go: Color is generated for both a.Color and a.Z; rename one of them with @go(name:)

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
